    description: "Found by the 2026-10-31 docstring staleness audit (dev 5f6b2af921): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_10312026/review and verify). Corpus impact not measured. _c_parameters (c.py:396-401) follows only the declarator field and stops at the outer function_declarator. int (*g(char *dst, const char *s))(int) gives parameters (int) and no out_parameter_call on g(b, \"x\"); a plain h(char *dst, ...) gets one. v07."  # f1d7
